  "narrative": "Scientific synthesis at iteration 10. H140 and H58 response deadlines are resolved. H140 validation R106, signed +0.112 with independent lower bound +0.053, independently confirms the CDKN2A-loss versus intact effect on dependency_MDM2 among TP53-wildtype cells. That lower bound is far above the task-relevant 10-percent scale benchmark of about 0.027 for MDM2, so H140 remains accepted and closed. H58 validation R107, signed +0.358 with independent lower bound +0.127, confirms the PTEN-loss versus intact effect on dependency_STAT3 in non-Avana screens, far above the STAT3 benchmark of about 0.028; H58 remains accepted and closed. H163 is the reversed PTEN-by-TP53 interaction claim for STAT3. Validation R133 is signed +0.009 with interval -0.204 to +0.222, so it is near null and very imprecise. Together with discovery R112, which was also wide, and the accepted direct strata showing positive PTEN effects in both TP53-loss and TP53-wildtype cells, this evidence does not establish a reliable clinically meaningful TP53 modification. I leave H163 unresolved because the interval does not exclude moderate effects, but I close it because further sparse interaction probes are unlikely to be decisive. The strongest supported findings are six dataset-only observational associations. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with markedly stronger SMARCA2 dependency, with independent validation and broad robustness across library, lineage, co-deletion, and screen-quality strata. Second, MSI-high status is associated with markedly stronger WRN dependency, with independent validation and robustness across lineage, library, Cas9, growth, serum, mutation-burden, and BRCA2 contexts. Third, KEAP1 loss is associated with markedly weaker NFE2L2 dependency, with independent validation and broad robustness across lineage, library, TP53, MYC, STK11, growth, serum, and screen-quality strata. Fourth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency, with independent validation overall and in both Avana and non-Avana library contexts, and strong direct strata including TP53-loss, TP53-wildtype, EMT, hypoxia, and STK11-loss cells. Fifth, TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency, with independent validation and multiple accepted biological strata. Sixth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, independently validated in the TP53-wildtype comparison and supported in many technical, lineage, MTAP, growth, and screen-quality strata. Negative or unsupported findings include the main matched-driver hypotheses: EGFR amplification with EGFR dependency, ERBB2 amplification with ERBB2 dependency, KRAS mutation with KRAS dependency, BRAF V600E with BRAF or RIT1 dependency, ARID1A loss with SMARCA2 dependency, MYC amplification with POLR2A/RPL11/USP7 dependency, and NF1 loss with BRAF or RIT1 dependency. Formal effect-modification claims remain generally unresolved or rejected: Avana-by-PTEN, PIK3CA-by-PTEN, TP53-by-PTEN, lineage modification of several accepted effects, and KRAS STK11/TP53 conditional interactions are not accepted. Several remaining unresolved contexts have been closed as sparse, redundant, or low priority to preserve analysis capacity. The most informative next analyses are the retained direct robustness and lineage strata for accepted effects: H81 squamous SMARCA2, H37/H38 SMARCA2 high-Cas9/high-aneuploidy, H60/H61/H65 STAT3 lineage and IFN contexts, and H75/H76/H78/H79 USP7 library and lineage contexts. These analyses test whether the accepted associations generalize across the main technical and histologic strata present in the supplied dataset. All conclusions remain observational associations in this dataset, not causal claims or statements of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 10 synthesis. Validated core dataset-only associations: SMARCA4 loss to stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high to stronger WRN dependency; KEAP1 loss to weaker NFE2L2 dependency; PTEN loss to stronger STAT3 dependency; TP53 loss to weaker USP7 dependency; CDKN2A loss to stronger MDM2 dependency in TP53-wildtype cells. H140 validation R106 and H58 validation R107 confirm key strata and remain accepted. H163 validation R133 is near-null and imprecise; no reliable TP53 modification of PTEN-STAT3 is established, so H163 is closed unresolved. Active analyses retained: H81 squamous SMARCA2; H37 and H38 SMARCA2 high Cas9 and high aneuploidy; H60 and H61 STAT3 lineage; H65 STAT3 IFN; H75 and H76 USP7 library; H78 and H79 USP7 lineage. Low-priority, sparse, redundant, driver-negative, or marker-only follow-ups are closed to focus analysis. No new proposals; use remaining analysis slots on the retained direct robustness strata. Avoid further KRAS, EGFR, ERBB2, BRAF, MYC, TMED10 marker, and sparse interaction probes unless a new signal emerges. All conclusions are limited to the supplied dataset and observational associations only."
